Contract:
REQUEST: Which vendor emails this month look suspicious? Flag them to the AP lead.
INTENDED OUTCOME: Review all vendor emails in the AP shared mailbox received this month (October 2026, through 2026-10-10), identify those with concrete 
fraud/suspicion indicators, verify what can be checked against read-only ERP vendor/bill data, and send the AP lead one alert/flag email with the findings.
DELIVERABLE TO USER: A single alert email sent from the AP shared mailbox to the AP lead listing each suspicious vendor email with message ID, sender, subject, 
received date, the suspicious indicator(s), and evidence (including any ERP comparison); if none are suspicious, an email stating none found.
CONSTRAINTS:
  - Do not modify, delete, forward, reply to, or mark any vendor email in the AP mailbox; only read them and send the final alert to the AP lead.
  - Do not click or execute attachments; download attachments to drive only for metadata/text inspection.
  - Restrict the review to vendor emails in the AP mailbox received between 2026-10-01 and 2026-10-10 inclusive.
  - Use ERP read-only APIs only; do not create, modify, or delete any ERP vendor, bill, or payment record.
  - Flag only emails with at least one concrete suspicious indicator; avoid reporting ordinary vendor email.
  - Preserve evidence for each flag: original message ID, sender, subject, date, relevant quote, and ERP comparison result.
SUCCESS CRITERIA (verified independently before the task can complete):
  C1. All vendor emails in the AP mailbox received between 2026-10-01 and 2026-10-10 have been inspected and classified.
  C2. Every flagged email has a concrete suspicious indicator documented (e.g. sender domain does not match ERP vendor contact/domain, payment/bank-change 
request, invoice number/amount/status mismatch against ERP bills, or dangerous attachment type/macros).
  C3. Exactly one alert email to the AP lead exists in the mailbox sent/outbox containing the suspicious-email list and evidence; if no suspicious emails were 
found, the alert states none found.
  C4. No ERP records or mailbox contents were changed as a result of this task; no bills/vendors/payments were created or altered and no vendor emails were 
deleted, replied to, or forwarded.
ASSUMPTIONS:
  - 'This month' means October 2026, specifically mail received from 2026-10-01 through 2026-10-10 (the portion existing as of today).
  - Vendor emails are external messages related to invoices, payments, vendor onboarding/changes, or statements; the AP mailbox contains these.
  - The AP lead's email address can be found in the AP mailbox or ERP; if not, fallback to requester.
  - Read-only ERP API is sufficient for verification; no write access is needed for this request.
PLAN:
  S1: Log in to the AP mailbox and list all inbox messages received from vendors between 2026-10-01 and 2026-10-10. (done when: A candidate list with message 
IDs, senders, subjects, and dates is captured from /mail.)
  S2: Determine the AP lead's name and email address from mailbox directory/address book or team info. (done when: AP lead recipient address is available for 
composing the alert.)
  S3: For each candidate vendor email, inspect message body and attachment metadata without executing anything; download attachments to drive only if needed for
inspection. (done when: Each candidate has content/attachment assessment and risk notes.)
  S4: For candidates with vendor-identity, payment-change, or invoice anomalies, query the ERP read-only API (/vendors, /bills) to verify expected vendor 
contacts/domains, invoice/bill status, and amount. (done when: Each relevant candidate has an ERP comparison result recorded.)
  S5: Classify each suspect as suspicious or not using concrete indicators and prepare the alert email with message ID, sender, subject, date, reason/evidence, 
and ERP comparison. (done when: A final alert draft/list is ready and reviewed for false positives.)
  S6: Send the alert email to the AP lead via /mail/compose, with the final list or a 'none found' statement. (done when: The alert is sent and confirmed in the
mailbox sent/outbox.)
